            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0274" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51/295</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1920-08-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 4, 1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received
                        August 25.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    Instruction No. 33, of June 19th, 1920, and previous correspondence, and to the
                    second paragraph of my telegram No. 290 of July 29th, 11 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">noon</hi>],<anchor n="9" xml:id="d146-f1"/> I have the
                    honor to enclose, herewith, translation-copy of a Pro-Memoria (No. 30162/177) of
                    August 3rd, from the R[oyal] Ministry of Foreign Affairs, regarding a loan from
                    the Italian Government to the Republic of Ecuador.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon Leavitt
                    Crosby</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d146-a1.xml" xpointer="d146-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
